  "behavior": [
    "One exhaustive TokenParser initializer receives an already-selected ordinary or independent parser copy and preserves every outer field clone operation.",
    "Deep copy no longer creates and then replaces a redundant ordinary ParserState; normal copies share the lexer and independent copies retain their own lexer.",
    "Private last-field witnesses count completed state clones and retirement after actual nonempty captures; they establish one clone and a two-state peak without allocator or byte claims.",
    "Public fixtures preserve committed captures/history, cached forcing, freshness, alternate EOS, remaining token allowance, configuration and terminal errors after source retirement.",
    "Logger clone intentionally starts a fresh log buffer as before. Raw lexer mutex poison behavior and infallible clone failure behavior are unchanged."
  ],
  "initial_failures": [],
  "limits": [
    "Removes one temporary state copy only; source/destination state overlap and independent lexer/caches still exist.",
    "No complete copy-byte bound, destination allocation authority, parser growth allowance or managed grammar admission is established.",
    "Witness counts completed ParserState values, not allocations, reserved bytes or peak process memory.",
    "All-feature and minimal parser runs overlap; total counts executions. Three external checkpoint fixtures remain ignored.",
    "Prompt-healing/rollback nondefault paths are preserved by field copying but not newly exercised by these fixtures.",
    "No allocator fault campaign, new released-checkpoint comparison, native numerical/distributed run or whole-process peak is claimed.",
    "Full family/path goal remains incomplete."
